  "releaseNotes": "Serialization output-method conformance (the HTML/XHTML/serialization-error path). HTML/XHTML output: URI-valued attributes (href/src/…) are NFC-normalized before percent-encoding non-ASCII octets; XHTML emits well-formed empty elements (br/) rather than HTML minimized tags; an existing http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" meta is replaced with the computed media-type and charset. Character maps now apply to attribute values as well as text (excluding URI-valued attributes under HTML/XHTML, where escape-uri-attributes governs). Invalid serialization parameters now raise the right W3C Serialization 4.0 errors — SESU0007 (unproducible encoding), SESU0011 (bad normalization-form), SEPM0004 (standalone/doctype with a non-single-document result), SEPM0009/SEPM0010 — and the undeclare-prefixes attribute is honored. Control characters (DEL, U+0080–U+009F, U+2028) in attribute values serialize as numeric character references instead of being emitted literally. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.2 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.5.4. No API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
